# ─── Server image (Dockerfile does `COPY server/ .`) ─────────────────────────
# Everything below is either personal data or dead weight, and until now all of
# it was baked into the deployed image.
#
# The JSON stores are the ones that matter: at RUNTIME every store is opened
# from config.DATA_DIR (/data, the Fly volume), never from the code directory,
# so these copies were never read — they simply travelled to the registry with
# real conversations, profiles and travel history inside them. Found on
# 2026-09-15 when a deploy reported a 728 MB build context.
server/conversations.json
server/profiles.json
server/user_memory.json
server/reminders.json
server/active_session.json
server/travel_prefs.json
server/known_places.json
server/bug_reports.json
server/judge_log.json
server/llm_usage.json
server/agents.json
server/sessions.json
server/cv_master.json
server/hr_pending.json

# 144 MB of virtualenv that the image rebuilds from requirements.txt anyway —
# and that `COPY server/ .` would lay on top of the pip-installed packages.
server/.venv/
server/__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/

# Tests and fixtures do not run in the production image.
server/tests/
server/personas/
server/personality_parity_fixture.json
